1 EXIT
    The EXIT command ends the command procedure it is in, and the
    command level that ran the procedure goes on.  At the terminal
    (command level 0), EXIT ends govax, as QUIT does.

    Syntax:

        EXIT [status]

    Parameters:

        status      An expression (see HELP SYMBOL EXPRESSIONS) whose
                    integer value is the procedure's status, the $STATUS
                    of the level that ran it.  A status that isn't a
                    success (an even number) has its message shown there,
                    unless its bit 28 says it has been shown already.
                    Without a status, the procedure's status is $STATUS,
                    marked as shown.  See HELP SYMBOL STATUS.

    Example:

        $ EXIT 1            ! end the procedure, successfully
